# The settings of docker-compose.yml. Copy this file to .env (git-ignored: it is never committed) with
#
#   bash jenkins/init-env.sh
#
# which fills in a random admin password. The password stays in .env: it is not printed anywhere, and the evidence of a build
# (docs/results/jenkins) is written without it. See jenkins/README.md.

# The one user of the controller. The password is generated by init-env.sh; an empty value stops docker compose.
JENKINS_ADMIN_ID=admin
JENKINS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Optional. The defaults are the lines below.
# The git repository the job reads (a clone, or a bare repository), mounted read-only at /repo. In a git worktree set it to
# another clone: a worktree's .git is a file that points outside the directory, and a container cannot follow it.
# PB_REPO=.
# The branch the job builds.
# PB_BRANCH=main
# Executors of the Linux agent: how many engines of the merge gate run at once (ADR-116).
# AGENT_EXECUTORS=2
